  "description": "GENERATED CANDIDATE - NOT RATIFIED. JoyCaption Beta One: a LLaVA image captioner (LlavaForConditionalGeneration) as one\ntransformers snapshot - SigLIP vision tower, multi_modal_projector and Llama language model,\nfour shards, flat BF16. WHOLE TREE, because there is no core to separate from the encoders here:\nthe endpoint binds the snapshot with one from_pretrained and the three sub-trees are one\ncheckpoint. Derived mechanically by tensorfs.generate from headers only - no tensor byte was read. beta-one: 743 tensors 48 declarations cover 743 tensors (23 singleton, 25 indexed) dtypes: BF16 x743. RATIFICATION OWED: (1) SCOPE CHECK owed against tensorfs#121: 'vision_tower.*' is a stock SigLIP spelling and\n'language_model.*' a stock Llama one, so the discriminating fact is the COMBINATION plus\n'multi_modal_projector.*'. Confirm no other served family ships the same three-prefix tree before\nthis document joins the global matcher set. (2) ROLES are mechanical (role == pattern). Rename any tensor whose bytes are the same bytes another packaging spells differently - that is the only thing that makes a cross-packaging derive possible instead of a refusal. (3) FUSIONS are undeclared. A header cannot see a fused axis, so a fused qkv/gate-up must be declared by a human reading the model's config (head count, hidden size); a wrong one is a ~90%-error split that never crashes. (4) SETS are undeclared (no subset-snapshot groups). (5) COMPONENT SCOPE is the caller's: declaring a shared encoder ties this document to every family that ships the same one (tensorfs#121).",
